module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.GeneratedQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.IsoClause
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.QuotientPresentation

/-!
# Tag 0801 for a graded ideal generated in one degree, from the general case

Work in Situation 01NN: a scheme `S`, a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra `𝒜` and a closed
immersion `i : Z ⟶ Proj_S(𝒜)`. Tag 0802 is stated with two inputs that are both the relative case
of Tag 0801: a `…GradedQuotientPresentation` of `Z` by *some* graded quotient of `𝒜`, and a
`…DegreeQuotientPresenter`, which is Tag 0801 again for the graded ideal `ℱ𝒜` generated by a
submodule `ℱ` of a single homogeneous piece.

**This file derives the second from the first.** Given a presentation of `Z` as `Proj_S(ℬ)` by a
degreewise surjection `ψ : 𝒜 ⟶ ℬ`, and given a quasi-coherent `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d` all of whose local
sections are equations for `Z` and which cuts `Z` out on the charts, `Z` is the relative Proj of
`𝒜/ℱ𝒜`. So `…DegreeQuotientPresenter 𝒜 i ψ` holds for the `ψ` of any graded quotient
presentation, and Tag 0802 needs only one Tag 0801 input rather than two.

## The route

`…CutsOutOnCharts` is a ring-level condition: over each affine open `U` of a cover of the base
and on each standard open `D₊(f)` of a covering family of the chart, the kernel of
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map (ψ.sectionHom U) f` is contained in the ideal `…chartIdeal`
that the local sections of `ℱ` generate there. Two observations turn that into the `iso` clause.

* The reverse containment is free from `…IsEquationSubmodule`: the local sections of `ℱ` lie in
  `ℱ𝒜`, hence in the kernel of `ψ` on sections, by `…generatedByDegree_le` at the sectionwise
  kernel of `ψ`. So the two *ring* kernels over `D₊(f)` agree — the kernel of `Away.map` of
  `ψ.sectionHom U` and the kernel of `Away.map` of the graded quotient map by `I_U`, the
  homogeneous ideal of sections `ℱ𝒜` cuts out.
* An equality of kernel ideal *sheaves* on an absolute `Proj` is tested on the standard opens,
  by `Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.ker_le_ker_of_app_awayMk`, and there each one is the kernel
  of `Away.map` by `Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.awayToSection_mem_ker_app_projMap_iff`.

That gives `(chartMap ψ U).ker = (chartMap (quotMk 𝒜 (ℱ𝒜)) U).ker` for each `U` of the cover,
which `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.KerChart.ker_eq_of_forall_chart` globalizes to
`i.ker = (quotAmbientHom 𝒜 (ℱ𝒜)).ker`, and
`…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.gradedQuotientPresentation_of_ker_eq` turns into the presentation. Its
kernel clause is `…isQuotientByDegreeSubmodule_quotMk`.

## Main results

* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ker_projMap_eq_of_ker_awayMap_eq`: two morphisms of absolute
  projective spectra out of graded quotients of one graded ring have the same kernel ideal sheaf
  as soon as the kernels of the induced maps of degree-zero localizations agree on a covering
  family of standard opens.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ker_chartMap_eq_ker_chartMap_quotMk`: the chart-level comparison.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.degreeQuotientPresenter_of_gradedQuotientPresentation`: **Tag 0801
  for a single-degree graded ideal, from Tag 0801 for a general one.**

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0802](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0802)

## Not done here

No Stacks tag is claimed. The relative case of Tag 0801 is still not proved: what is removed is
the *second* of the two assumptions of the relative case, not the first. A
`…GradedQuotientPresentation` of the closed subscheme remains an input, and the `Not done here`
section of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/IsoClause.lean` records what
its construction is blocked on.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open HomogeneousLocalization
